# SLH-L-0002 — The SLH nomenclature, 2026-11-23

The project gets its name, its documents get names that say what they are,
and the repository gets a memory that every session reads first.

## The change

| | |
|---|---|
| Branch | `feat/rudimentary` |
| Follows | commit `c79e3b9`, the change recorded in [SLH-L-0001](SLH-L-0001-2026-11-23-the-rudimentary-method.hmd) |
| Size | 28 files: 10 renamed, 10 new, 8 corrected. About 800 lines added |
| Touches | `doc/`, `.loops/` and `CLAUDE.md` only. No card, query, script or proof was changed |
| Worked on by | Bob, Carol, Dave, and Alice as observer, in the discussion SLH-D-0002 |

## Objectives

1. **Name the project.** Strange Loops in HyperMarkdown, SLH.
2. **Name every indexed document by one rule,** `SLH-<letter>-<id>`, so that
   a name alone says which project and which kind of document.
3. **Keep the user's standing decisions where every agent reads them,** in
   the repository and not in a tool's private store.
4. **Say in plain words what the project is for.**
5. **Do it with the workers in parallel,** each job planned and inspected.

## Arrived at

| Kind | Letter | Documents |
|---|---|---|
| Proposal | `P` | `SLH-P-0001` |
| Story | `S` | `SLH-S-0001` |
| Issue | `I` | `SLH-I-0001`, `SLH-I-0002` |
| Discussion | `D` | `SLH-D-0001`, `SLH-D-0002` |
| Ledger entry | `L` | `SLH-L-0001`, `SLH-L-0002` |
| Memory | `M` | `SLH-M-0001`, `SLH-M-0002` |

Every kind has an index that lists its documents. Every relative link in the
repository resolves. Git records each renamed file as a rename, so its
history follows it.

## Accomplished

- **Bob** renamed the proposal and wrote the index of proposals, which the
  folder did not have.
- **Dave** renamed the two issues, corrected the board, the index and the
  roadmap, and repaired seven links that had been dead since the wiki was
  split into vaults.
- **Carol** renamed the first discussion, brought the rules and both prompts
  in line with numbered discussions, and added the list of discussions.
- **Alice** renamed the story and the first ledger entry, created the
  memories folder with its first two memories, put the instruction to read
  them at the top of `CLAUDE.md`, wrote "In plain words" into the story, and
  inspected the four jobs.

## Decisions

| Decision | Decided by |
|---|---|
| The project is called **Strange Loops in HyperMarkdown, SLH** | the user |
| A document indexed under `doc/` is named `SLH-<letter>-<id>`, with `P`, `S`, `I` and `D` for proposal, story, issue and discussion | the user |
| `M` for a memory and `L` for a ledger entry | proposed by the observer, approved by the user |
| The id is a four-digit number that is never reused. A short name follows it. A discussion and a ledger entry carry their date between the two | proposed by the observer, approved by the user |
| A discussion is a folder, and its id names the folder | the user |
| The concept cards, the indexes and the methodology documents are not renamed | proposed by the observer, approved by the user |
| `doc/memories/` exists, and every session reads it before anything else | the user |
| The memories in the repository come first. An agent's private memory is secondary and gives way where the two differ | the user |
| A memory is written only on the user's word, never from an agent's own conclusion | the observer, in the form of the folder |
| A discussion is closed when its folder holds a consolidation | Carol, confirmed by the observer |
| A job for several agents starts from a fixed map and from sets of files that do not overlap | the observer; approved by the user as the plan |

## Sidetracks

**None that cost anything.** The job was planned before it was started and
ran without two agents meeting in one file.

**Small ones.** The observer's inspection script first reported twelve old
names that were not there. It had been written to strip the new prefix
before searching, which turned every new name back into an old one. It was
corrected before any job was judged by it. The index of discussions listed
no discussions, which the inspection found and Carol repaired.

**One thing done beyond the brief.** Dave repaired seven dead links in the
issues that the rename had not caused. They were in Dave's set, the
inspection would have failed on them, and Dave said so in the report.

## Not done

- **Everything left open by SLH-L-0001.** This change built nothing of the
  system. The health figure is still not computed.
- **Stale prose.** The issues and the roadmap still describe a `wiki/` vault
  in running text.
- **Link texts.** Some links still describe their target in words where the
  memory asks for its name.
- **The private memory about cards** has not been moved into
  `doc/memories/`.
- **The statuses of a proposal,** as Bob wrote them, wait for the user's
  word.
